m canadian currency to the portraits  hung in arenas well new polling from  ipsos confirms the depths of her  relationship with canada 82 of canadians  were happy with how she conducted  herself as monarch although her heir  king charles iii clearly has his work  cut out for him in the eyes of canadians  it proves that what we've known for a  long time that it was the queen who was  holding the monarchy together  when it comes to favorability numbers  king charles and queen consort camilla  are low and their lack of popularity has  in part reopened the discussion about  the king's role as canada's head of  state even if the survey does show  canadians don't strongly agree one way  or the other the only thing that's been  keeping us a monarchy aside from  obviously the popularity of the queen is  apathy  and as long as people don't care  and aren't interested then we'll  continue to be a monarchy well people  care but the question is how much when  weighing the pros and cons canadians see  the monarchy as something that helps  define our identity while helping to  keep us distinct from the us but flip  the coin and canadians see the royals as  nothing more than celebrities with  uncomfortable ties to colonialism you  have to say to yourself okay  if we're going to do away with the  monarchy what are we going to replace it  with and while canadians are clearly  conflicted former lieutenant governor of  ontario david only says the  constitutional requirement to have the  house of commons senate in all 10  provinces unanimously consent to sever  ties makes it a long shot when you think  of the problems facing canada that we  have today  where does the priority fit for  you know ending our relationship with  the monarchy  is it in the top 10 the top 20. i think  that's a companion  survey i'd like to see  where does it fit it might not be a  pressing issue but it's one that won't  go away mike drolite global news toronto  and the funeral for the queen is on  monday at we